WEBVTT

00:02.118 --> 00:03.953
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:04.037 --> 00:05.455
I don't know how it happened,

00:05.538 --> 00:09.918
but you seem to have some
communion with this island, John.

00:10.001 --> 00:12.462
And that makes you very, very important.

00:12.545 --> 00:15.507
In time, you'll have a better
understanding of things.

00:18.510 --> 00:19.594
Kwon is pregnant.

00:19.677 --> 00:22.597
- <i>The foetus is healthy...</i>
- What's that?

00:22.680 --> 00:25.475
Juliet is gathering information
for us at your camp.

00:25.558 --> 00:31.512
She's determining if any women are
pregnant. Then we're going to take them.

00:31.606 --> 00:35.026
Juliet is a mole.
She's working for Ben.

00:37.278 --> 00:39.739
- We're moving.
- Moving? Where are we going?

00:39.823 --> 00:43.993
We are not going anywhere, John.
You are going to stay behind.

00:44.077 --> 00:45.912
We'll leave a trail, one you can track.

00:45.995 --> 00:50.083
And John, unless you're carrying your
father's body on your back,

00:51.209 --> 00:52.711
don't bother.

00:58.717 --> 01:00.468
Come on, damn it, push!

01:04.514 --> 01:06.589
Something's wrong. I can't...

01:08.601 --> 01:12.856
Emily, you can do this! Now, push!

01:12.939 --> 01:15.150
Come on, come on, baby.

01:15.233 --> 01:16.860
You can do it, now, come on.

01:16.943 --> 01:19.988
Come on, there you go. Come on.

01:26.119 --> 01:30.832
It's a boy. You did it.

01:30.915 --> 01:32.907
It hurts.

01:39.382 --> 01:41.593
Oh. You did it.

01:44.763 --> 01:47.004
Oh, my God. Roger, it hurts.

01:47.098 --> 01:48.214
Emily...

01:51.936 --> 01:56.649
Emily. No one knows we're out here.
We gotta get back, OK, honey?

01:56.733 --> 01:58.975
Can you hold on to the baby?

01:59.069 --> 02:02.655
Emily! Can you hold the baby?
Hold him tight.

02:15.668 --> 02:17.170
Hey! Help!

02:18.380 --> 02:19.412
Help.

02:19.506 --> 02:20.924
Help!

02:21.758 --> 02:22.842
Help!

02:26.346 --> 02:28.181
Help me...

02:28.264 --> 02:30.558
Hey, what happened, man?

02:30.642 --> 02:35.386
We were hiking. She went into labour.
She wasn't due yet. She's bleeding.

02:35.480 --> 02:38.566
We'll put her in the car, OK?
We'll get you to the hospital.

02:38.650 --> 02:40.694
OK, OK, honey...

02:40.777 --> 02:44.114
OK, it's all right,
let's keep her warm, all right?

02:44.197 --> 02:46.408
- How's the baby?
- Fine, I guess. I don't know.

02:47.409 --> 02:49.734
Roger...Roger...

02:49.828 --> 02:52.747
- I'm right here...
- Call him Benjamin.

02:53.248 --> 02:55.125
Stay with me...

02:57.627 --> 03:00.505
Stay with me. Emily!

03:03.633 --> 03:06.636
Emily! Oh, God, no!

03:14.352 --> 03:15.937
What ya got there?

03:16.020 --> 03:20.681
It's a birthday present.
Mine just happens to be today.

03:21.735 --> 03:24.946
You do remember birthdays,
don't you, Richard?

03:25.655 --> 03:28.283
So, do you want me to bring
the tape back to Juliet?

03:29.075 --> 03:30.108
What?

03:30.201 --> 03:34.205
The tape with instructions for Juliet.
Do you want it at the Medical Station?

03:34.289 --> 03:37.625
I recorded it yesterday, before we left.
I thought you took it.

03:37.709 --> 03:41.629
- No.
- Where's Tom?

03:41.713 --> 03:47.093
Tom? Have you seen my recorder?

04:11.785 --> 04:16.081
You said that if I killed my father,

04:16.164 --> 04:20.001
you'd tell me everything
I wanted to know about the island.

04:24.130 --> 04:27.050
So, why don't you
start at the beginning?

04:49.155 --> 04:51.647
I know I promised to tell you
everything, John,

04:51.741 --> 04:57.122
and I wish it was as simple as me taking
out a dusty old book and opening it up.

05:07.424 --> 05:09.008
But it's not that simple.

05:09.092 --> 05:11.386
How about you just tell me.

05:12.554 --> 05:16.224
You probably think I'm the leader
of this little community.

05:16.307 --> 05:19.759
But that's not entirely true.

05:19.853 --> 05:22.063
We all answer to someone, John.

05:22.147 --> 05:23.815
And who might that be?

05:25.608 --> 05:27.652
His name is Jacob.

05:27.736 --> 05:30.947
OK, then, take me to Jacob.

05:31.031 --> 05:32.407
I can't do that.

05:34.534 --> 05:35.702
Where are you going?

05:35.785 --> 05:38.538
If you don't want to take me,
maybe someone else will.

05:38.621 --> 05:40.582
I'll just go and ask Richard.

05:40.665 --> 05:44.033
Why would Richard take you?
He doesn't talk to Jacob.

05:44.127 --> 05:45.795
- Well, who talks to him?
- I do.

05:45.879 --> 05:47.787
- You're the only one?
- That's right.

05:47.881 --> 05:49.758
And no one else knows where he is?

05:49.841 --> 05:52.594
I was born here on this island.

05:52.677 --> 05:54.919
I'm one of the last that was.

05:55.013 --> 05:59.590
Most of these people you see, I brought
them here. So, Jacob talks to me, John.

06:00.018 --> 06:03.521
He tells me what to do, trusts me.

06:03.605 --> 06:07.776
And no one else has ever seen him.

06:07.859 --> 06:11.144
- That's right.
- How convenient.

06:11.446 --> 06:16.076
You know what I think, Ben?
I think there is no Jacob.

06:16.159 --> 06:18.370
I think people are idiots
if they believe

06:18.453 --> 06:20.497
you take orders from someone else.

06:20.580 --> 06:26.461
You are the man behind the curtain,
the Wizard of Oz.

06:28.171 --> 06:29.839
And you're a liar.

06:31.674 --> 06:33.968
And what might you base
that theory on, John?

06:34.052 --> 06:39.516
Because if you were telling the truth,
your hand wouldn't be shaking.

07:16.511 --> 07:17.595
Namaste.

07:19.347 --> 07:21.255
- Thanks.
- Namaste.

07:22.767 --> 07:26.104
Hey, welcome to the island, man.
Namaste.

07:26.187 --> 07:30.233
- Namaste, yeah.
- So, what do ya think?

07:30.316 --> 07:34.654
Well, this is some place. Thanks again
for the opportunity, Mr Goodspeed.

07:34.738 --> 07:36.114
- Horace, please.
- Horace.

07:36.197 --> 07:38.825
- And this must be Ben.
- Yeah.

07:38.908 --> 07:41.150
Mr Goodspeed was there
the day you were born.

07:41.244 --> 07:43.569
Yes, I was.

07:43.663 --> 07:47.083
He's doing us a big favour here,
gave your old man a job.

07:48.168 --> 07:49.544
He don't say much.

07:49.627 --> 07:54.372
That's OK. I bet he will when
he has something to say. Right, Ben?

07:54.758 --> 07:58.511
Hey, you hungry, kiddo?

07:58.595 --> 08:02.766
Great. Tell you what, after you're
done processing, we'll have some lunch.

08:02.849 --> 08:03.881
How's that sound?

08:03.975 --> 08:06.551
- Yeah, thanks you.
- You're gonna love it here.

08:08.104 --> 08:11.608
<i>Welcome to the island.</i>
<i>For your own comfort and safety</i>,

08:11.691 --> 08:14.944
<i>we ask that you stay within the confines</i>
<i>of your new quarters.</i>

08:15.028 --> 08:19.199
<i>Our barracks are surrounded by</i>
<i>a high frequency sonar fence</i>

08:19.282 --> 08:23.411
<i>to protect us from the island's</i>
<i>abundant and diverse wildlife.</i>

08:23.495 --> 08:25.955
<i>You are now a member</i>
<i>of the Dharma Initiative.</i>

08:26.039 --> 08:29.323
What kind of wildlife you think
this fence is protecting us from?

08:29.417 --> 08:32.754
- Roger Linus? Roger Linus?
- Yeah.

08:32.837 --> 08:34.996
Every <i>morning</i>, <i>you will be given</i>
<i>a new code</i>,

08:35.090 --> 08:37.634
<i>which will allow you to cross</i>
<i>outside the fence.</i>

08:39.344 --> 08:43.014
<i>There are properties on this island</i>
<i>that exist nowhere else on Earth.</i>

08:43.098 --> 08:45.892
<i>Our mission is to study these properties</i>

08:45.975 --> 08:50.605
<i>for the betterment of mankind and</i>
<i>advancement of world peace.</i>

08:53.149 --> 08:55.641
<i>Should you be assigned</i>
<i>to zoological studies...</i>

08:55.735 --> 08:59.406
Hey. You're new, huh?

09:01.616 --> 09:02.648
I'm Annie.

09:04.577 --> 09:06.788
Want one?

09:09.374 --> 09:12.168
We can have as many as we want.

09:12.460 --> 09:18.258
"Work Man"?
What is this? "Work Man"?

09:19.467 --> 09:21.511
- I'm a janitor?
- I'm sorry, Mr Linus.

09:21.594 --> 09:25.265
Goodspeed told me you people were
doing experiments, changing the world.

09:25.348 --> 09:26.975
I didn't come here to clean up.

09:27.058 --> 09:30.145
If anything else opens up,
you can feel free to apply for it.

09:33.398 --> 09:35.640
Come on.

09:38.445 --> 09:41.698
Dude, you know, this can't
be worse than haggis.

09:46.411 --> 09:48.621
Hey. Sayid.

09:52.333 --> 09:54.909
- What happened to you?
- I was with Locke.

09:55.462 --> 09:58.339
- Well, where is he?
- He went back.

09:58.423 --> 09:59.455
Back where?

09:59.549 --> 10:03.000
With them. Don't ask me where the hell
it is 'cause it don't matter.

10:03.094 --> 10:07.098
What does matter, is this.

10:17.108 --> 10:20.476
Where is Ben? Where is he?

10:25.241 --> 10:27.285
I thought you were dead.

10:28.703 --> 10:31.790
I'm fortunate the pylons
were not set to a lethal level.

10:35.251 --> 10:39.036
- What is he doing here?
- It's all right.

10:39.130 --> 10:42.050
He's the one who tried to kill me.

10:43.426 --> 10:46.179
He's with us now.

10:46.262 --> 10:47.806
Where have you been, Mikhail?

10:47.889 --> 10:50.934
I encountered several
of his people in the jungle.

10:51.017 --> 10:53.144
They had an injured woman with them.

10:53.228 --> 10:55.803
Apparently, she just
parachuted onto the island.

10:55.897 --> 10:58.566
- What?
- Her helo crashed in the water.

10:58.650 --> 11:03.478
She says her ship is approximately
130 klicks to the west of us.

11:03.571 --> 11:06.366
- She has a radio-telephone.
- Where is she now?

11:06.449 --> 11:09.619
I assume they have taken her
back to their camp.

11:09.703 --> 11:13.123
We'll be visiting their camp day
after tomorrow. We'll take care of it.

11:13.206 --> 11:15.417
Day after tomorrow?
We have to go now.

11:15.500 --> 11:17.492
Ben's not going anywhere with you.

11:18.878 --> 11:21.840
- Excuse me?
- He and I are going to see Jacob.

11:29.139 --> 11:30.932
Please tell me this isn't true.

11:37.355 --> 11:41.568
I'm sorry, I have to deal with this now,
John. Our excursion will have to wait.

11:43.361 --> 11:46.948
Since when do you explain
yourself to him, an outsider?

11:50.035 --> 11:51.786
Tom!

11:52.495 --> 11:53.913
Richard!

12:05.800 --> 12:08.803
So, when do we leave?

12:13.058 --> 12:16.843
You know, you didn't have to beat
Mikhail senseless to make your point.

12:17.771 --> 12:19.929
Yes, I did.

12:20.023 --> 12:22.515
Locke...

12:25.987 --> 12:27.572
I hear you're gonna go see Jacob.

12:29.032 --> 12:31.826
You're gonna need this.

12:37.916 --> 12:38.948
Thanks.

12:46.466 --> 12:48.374
Happy birthday, Dad.

13:01.940 --> 13:05.224
So, once water is
added to the bicarbonate,

13:05.318 --> 13:08.738
we will get our very own
volcanic reaction.

13:09.614 --> 13:10.646
Yes?

13:10.740 --> 13:13.316
Is that what happened to
the volcano on this island?

13:13.410 --> 13:17.330
Exactly, Annie, but that
was a long time ago.

13:17.414 --> 13:19.541
OK, so let's get
ourselves an eruption.

13:19.624 --> 13:21.084
Oh, cool.

13:21.167 --> 13:26.245
Just add water and, voila.
Now, I know it's not lava, but...

13:27.549 --> 13:29.217
What was that?

13:33.471 --> 13:35.630
OK, everyone into your positions.

13:39.102 --> 13:42.804
That's right, all together.
Annie, lock the back door, please.

13:45.775 --> 13:48.319
Ben, come on, honey, you've gotta move.

13:49.070 --> 13:50.321
Ben!

13:54.617 --> 13:56.244
Come on.

14:01.458 --> 14:04.169
Don't worry, it's just the hostiles.

14:06.046 --> 14:07.130
We'll be OK.

14:08.923 --> 14:10.008
Get down!

14:13.219 --> 14:15.545
Hey, man. Heard you
ran into a little trouble.

14:15.638 --> 14:19.934
We're driving back from the Flame
and we hear this huge explosion.

14:20.018 --> 14:22.593
Next thing I know,
there's a siren wailing

14:22.687 --> 14:24.647
and we're driving through a shoot-out.

14:24.731 --> 14:27.275
We're having some
skirmishes with the natives.

14:27.359 --> 14:28.735
What do you mean, "natives"?

14:28.818 --> 14:30.945
Well, we're not exactly sure
who they are.

14:31.029 --> 14:33.323
Well, this ain't what I signed up for.

14:33.406 --> 14:37.702
Roger, I did you a favour, man.
You were having trouble finding work.

14:37.786 --> 14:40.663
Don't forget about Ben.
He's getting a quality education.

14:40.747 --> 14:42.738
I don't give a damn about his education.

14:42.832 --> 14:46.617
If I'm gonna get shot at, I want
hazard pay! I want another thirty grand.

14:46.711 --> 14:47.743
Calm down, man.

14:47.837 --> 14:51.508
And don't try to tell me you
don't have it, you hear me?

14:52.967 --> 14:54.594
Get the hell out of my house!

15:05.897 --> 15:07.774
I thought I told you to go to bed.

15:35.552 --> 15:38.836
- She's not here.
- I noticed.

15:39.305 --> 15:43.007
- What are you doing?
- Looking for Juliet.

15:43.101 --> 15:45.854
You're not gonna find her in there.
She left with Jack.

15:45.937 --> 15:47.272
Juliet left with Jack?

15:47.355 --> 15:49.733
He took off right after
I told him about Naomi.

15:49.816 --> 15:51.359
Who's Naomi?

15:51.443 --> 15:53.194
And why would you do that, Kate?

15:53.278 --> 15:55.436
Because she's hurt,
because he's a doctor,

15:55.530 --> 15:57.365
and because he has a right to know.

15:58.033 --> 15:59.993
- Where is he now?
- I don't know, Sayid.

16:00.076 --> 16:01.953
Of course you don't.

16:02.037 --> 16:04.998
It might be time for you to
tell everybody else about Naomi.

16:05.081 --> 16:06.249
Play her the tape.

16:07.876 --> 16:09.753
What tape?

16:15.175 --> 16:18.543
Something you should know, John,
before we go...

16:19.971 --> 16:22.380
...whether or not you think
he's the Wizard of Oz,

16:22.474 --> 16:25.925
I can assure you that
Jacob is very, very real.

16:29.397 --> 16:32.484
And we're going to go see him,
and he's not going to like it.

16:33.360 --> 16:38.907
In fact, I have a feeling
he's going to be very angry.

16:39.908 --> 16:45.038
That's why my hand was shaking, because
this is not a man you go and see.

16:45.121 --> 16:47.791
This is a man who summons you.

16:49.959 --> 16:53.327
Well, I guess there's
a first time for everything.

17:34.087 --> 17:38.174
It's us. That's you, and that's me.

17:41.136 --> 17:43.346
Now we never have to be
away from each other.

17:48.226 --> 17:50.218
Happy birthday, Ben.

17:51.813 --> 17:54.774
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

18:40.987 --> 18:42.979
It's your birthday.

18:45.825 --> 18:47.786
Sorry I forgot.

18:51.873 --> 18:55.460
Kinda hard to celebrate
on the day you killed your mom.

18:56.711 --> 19:00.215
She was just seven months pregnant.
We went for a hike.

19:00.298 --> 19:03.885
But you had to come early...

19:04.844 --> 19:08.713
Now she's gone,

19:08.807 --> 19:12.560
and I'm stuck here
on this island... with you.

19:24.239 --> 19:26.908
Happy birthday, Ben.

19:51.808 --> 19:53.184
Mom?

19:59.024 --> 20:01.234
Ben, don't!

20:04.946 --> 20:09.325
- Mom.
- It's not time yet, Benjamin.

20:16.416 --> 20:17.792
Mom!

20:21.254 --> 20:22.286
Mom.

20:56.998 --> 21:01.742
- Let's go, John.
- John.

21:10.053 --> 21:12.263
So, what, the world thinks we're dead?

21:12.347 --> 21:14.338
- That's not important.
- Not important?

21:14.432 --> 21:17.519
- What do you mean, not important?
- Excuse me...

21:18.186 --> 21:20.647
I'm sorry, don't you people
want to be rescued?

21:20.730 --> 21:22.722
We kept her a secret to keep her safe.

21:22.816 --> 21:24.275
Safe from what, Sayid?

21:24.359 --> 21:25.475
Safe from Jack.

21:26.611 --> 21:30.699
He spent a week with the Others, and
he brought one of them back with him.

21:30.782 --> 21:33.274
Here, amongst us.

21:33.368 --> 21:36.246
And every time we try to get answers
from this woman,

21:36.329 --> 21:37.997
he prevents her from giving them.

21:38.081 --> 21:42.992
But, it's Jack.
He would never do anything to hurt us.

21:43.086 --> 21:46.214
And Juliet,
I believe she is a good person.

21:46.297 --> 21:49.342
Good person?
And you're basing that on what?

21:49.426 --> 21:53.680
It wouldn't involve her taking you to
one of their medical stations, would it?

21:56.224 --> 21:57.934
- How...
- <i>Kwon is pregnant.</i>

21:58.017 --> 22:01.771
<i>The foetus is healthy and was</i>
<i>conceived on island with her husband.</i>

22:01.855 --> 22:04.607
<i>He was sterile before they got here.</i>

22:04.691 --> 22:07.569
<i>I'm working on getting samples</i>
<i>from the other women.</i>

22:07.652 --> 22:10.572
<i>I should have Austen's soon.</i>
<i>I'll report when I know more.</i>

22:10.655 --> 22:12.897
Where'd you get that?

22:14.159 --> 22:16.870
- Where have you been, Jack?
- I asked you where you got it.

22:16.953 --> 22:19.164
You're in a position
to ask us questions?

22:19.247 --> 22:21.082
- Turn the tape over.
- Stay out of it!

22:21.166 --> 22:23.793
You want to burn me at the stake?
Here I am. But first,

22:23.877 --> 22:26.004
turn the tape over, press play.

22:36.139 --> 22:37.390
<i>Juliet</i>, <i>it's Ben.</i>

22:37.474 --> 22:41.519
<i>I'm sending three teams to extract</i>
<i>Kwon the night after tomorrow.</i>

22:41.603 --> 22:43.678
<i>We won't have time</i>
<i>to run Austen's sample</i>,

22:43.772 --> 22:46.608
<i>so if you determine that she</i>
<i>or anyone else is pregnant</i>,

22:46.691 --> 22:51.269
<i>mark their tents and</i>
<i>we'll take them</i>, <i>too.</i>

22:51.363 --> 22:53.031
<i>Good luck.</i>

22:58.787 --> 23:01.362
The night I saw your baby
on the ultrasound,

23:01.456 --> 23:03.781
I told Jack what they were making me do.

23:05.877 --> 23:07.587
Why didn't you tell us?

23:07.670 --> 23:11.289
Because I hadn't decided
what to do about it yet.

23:11.383 --> 23:12.717
Yet?

23:20.225 --> 23:23.395
I think we've got some
catching up to do.

24:39.220 --> 24:40.597
Mom?

24:47.562 --> 24:49.105
Mom?

24:50.982 --> 24:52.014
Mom!

24:52.901 --> 24:54.361
Mom!

24:54.736 --> 24:56.696
Mom!

25:15.882 --> 25:19.500
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Whoa, hey, hey.

25:19.594 --> 25:22.389
I didn't mean to scare you...
Wait. Are you lost? Wait.

25:26.309 --> 25:27.685
Are you one of them?

25:28.603 --> 25:31.481
- One of who?
- A hostile.

25:34.567 --> 25:37.362
Do you even know what that word means?

25:37.445 --> 25:38.478
What's your name?

25:38.571 --> 25:40.615
- Ben.
- Ben?

25:40.699 --> 25:44.035
You wanna tell me what you're doing
in the jungle all by yourself?

25:46.621 --> 25:51.084
I left home, and...
I'm looking for my mom.

25:51.167 --> 25:54.838
- You think she's out here?
- You wouldn't believe me.

25:55.588 --> 25:56.965
Try me.

25:59.259 --> 26:00.541
She's dead.

26:06.057 --> 26:08.852
Did she die here? On the island?

26:08.935 --> 26:12.637
No. When I was a baby.

26:13.732 --> 26:17.819
Did you see her... out here, Ben?
In the jungle?

26:19.696 --> 26:21.072
She talked to me.

26:23.783 --> 26:25.201
What'd she say?

26:25.285 --> 26:26.870
That I couldn't come with her.

26:28.496 --> 26:30.874
She said it wasn't time yet.

26:37.797 --> 26:40.842
You should go home now.
Your people will be looking for you.

26:40.925 --> 26:42.834
I don't want to go back there!

26:44.387 --> 26:46.222
I hate it there.

26:50.769 --> 26:53.177
Take me with you.

26:54.564 --> 26:58.902
Maybe that can happen. Maybe.

26:58.985 --> 27:03.281
If it that's what you really want, Ben,
I want you to think about that.

27:05.575 --> 27:10.455
And you're going to have to be very,
very patient.

27:31.643 --> 27:33.937
We're here.

27:46.282 --> 27:48.691
You'll want to turn off
your flashlight, John.

27:48.785 --> 27:49.901
Why?

27:53.289 --> 27:56.626
Jacob feels the same way
about technology as you do.

28:33.997 --> 28:36.666
Once I open this door,
there's no turning back.

28:39.878 --> 28:42.036
Are you sure this is what you want?

28:50.346 --> 28:51.931
So be it.

28:54.559 --> 28:57.312
Jacob?

28:57.395 --> 28:59.272
I'm here with John Locke.

29:00.273 --> 29:02.650
We're coming in now.

29:25.215 --> 29:27.540
Jacob...

29:28.760 --> 29:30.261
This is John.

29:32.347 --> 29:34.672
Aren't you going to say hello, John?

29:37.268 --> 29:41.773
- What?
- I told you he wouldn't.

29:41.856 --> 29:44.432
Who... What are you talking about?

29:45.652 --> 29:47.612
You can't see him?

29:47.696 --> 29:50.532
- See who?
- Jacob.

29:52.450 --> 29:55.161
He's sitting right here...
in this chair.

29:55.245 --> 29:57.372
Yes, I know, but he insisted.

29:59.916 --> 30:04.087
- What is this?
- You wanted the secrets of the island.

30:04.170 --> 30:08.633
Well, here they are. This is the man
who can answer every single...

30:10.510 --> 30:15.640
I am not. He made me bring him here.
Did you think that that was my...

30:15.724 --> 30:17.715
- Sorry... May I finish?
- You're crazy.

30:20.603 --> 30:21.803
Excuse me?

30:23.356 --> 30:27.610
You don't know anything about the
island, do you? You just made it all up.

30:27.694 --> 30:31.281
- Jacob, please, I can't hear him if...
- Stop. Stop it. Shut up!

30:33.950 --> 30:37.652
Are you putting on a show for me?

30:37.746 --> 30:38.913
Or do you...

30:40.790 --> 30:43.001
Do you really think
there's someone there?

30:44.002 --> 30:46.463
I know there's someone there.

30:50.884 --> 30:53.209
You don't know anything.

31:01.644 --> 31:04.773
I'm sorry you feel that way, John.

31:06.483 --> 31:10.070
And I'm sorry that you're
too limited to see.

31:10.153 --> 31:11.946
You're pathetic.

31:15.992 --> 31:19.204
Help me.

31:26.711 --> 31:28.505
What did you just say?

31:29.672 --> 31:32.300
I... I didn't say anything.

31:32.384 --> 31:37.514
Oh, yes you did. I heard you.
You said...

31:57.492 --> 31:59.400
That's enough! You've had your fun!

32:49.836 --> 32:51.119
What was that?

32:56.134 --> 32:59.054
That was Jacob.

33:06.478 --> 33:11.608
What did you hear in there, John?
What did Jacob say to you?

33:13.735 --> 33:18.865
- He didn't say anything to me. You did.
- What are you talking about?

33:18.948 --> 33:21.159
There is no Jacob, Ben.

33:21.242 --> 33:25.455
I'm not gonna be taken in by the
little... show you put on last night.

33:25.538 --> 33:29.667
You're a fraud. And it's time
your people were told the truth.

33:31.169 --> 33:33.838
And this is not the way we came.

33:35.090 --> 33:39.667
I'm taking us back another way.
I wanted to show you something first.

33:39.761 --> 33:42.138
I've seen enough.

33:42.222 --> 33:43.848
You know, John, you're not wrong.

33:43.932 --> 33:46.090
Some of the things I've told you...

33:46.184 --> 33:49.552
...some of the things I've told
everybody... are simply not true.

33:49.646 --> 33:51.314
Like what?

33:51.398 --> 33:55.443
Well, for starters,
I wasn't born on this island.

33:56.569 --> 33:58.321
Then where did you come from?

34:00.990 --> 34:02.617
That's what I want to show you.

34:53.877 --> 34:55.754
Morning.

34:55.837 --> 35:00.498
OK, wait. Put it right...
right down there.

35:02.427 --> 35:03.887
What's your problem now?

35:04.596 --> 35:07.171
You're usually Chatty Cathy
in the morning.

35:07.265 --> 35:08.641
It's my birthday.

35:12.687 --> 35:15.356
I don't know why I keep
fooling myself into thinking

35:15.440 --> 35:18.526
that one of these years
you're actually going to remember.

35:21.363 --> 35:23.437
Well, I'll tell you what,

35:23.531 --> 35:28.912
all we gotta do this morning
is run this stuff out to Pearl Station.

35:28.995 --> 35:32.999
Why don't we go up to the mesa,
drink some beers?

35:35.835 --> 35:41.049
Have some... I don't know,
father and son time?

35:44.010 --> 35:48.181
- I'd like that.
- OK.

36:02.696 --> 36:04.364
Well...

36:05.573 --> 36:08.118
You sure can't say
it ain't beautiful.

36:21.047 --> 36:22.924
Do you really blame me?

36:23.007 --> 36:24.592
What?

36:26.261 --> 36:29.139
Do you really think
it's my fault that she died?

36:33.351 --> 36:35.927
What do I know?

36:40.191 --> 36:43.862
Why do you keep looking at your watch?
You got a date?

36:44.779 --> 36:45.812
Listen...

36:48.283 --> 36:52.068
...if it makes you feel any better...

36:52.162 --> 36:56.499
...I will do my best
to remember your birthday next year.

36:59.544 --> 37:02.547
I don't think that's gonna happen, Dad.

37:04.340 --> 37:05.842
What do you mean?

37:05.925 --> 37:10.722
You know, I've missed her, too.
Maybe as much as you have.

37:10.805 --> 37:14.976
But the difference is,
that for as long as I can remember,

37:15.060 --> 37:17.468
I've had to put up with you.

37:19.564 --> 37:25.320
And doing that required
a tremendous amount of patience.

37:32.035 --> 37:34.412
Goodbye, Dad.

37:42.545 --> 37:43.578
Ben?

39:56.012 --> 40:00.183
You want us to go get his body?

40:04.354 --> 40:06.064
No, leave him out there.

40:29.129 --> 40:31.589
This is where I came from, John.

40:34.843 --> 40:40.598
These are my people.
The Dharma Initiative.

40:42.308 --> 40:45.437
They came here seeking harmony.

40:47.605 --> 40:51.985
But they couldn't even coexist
with the island's original inhabitants.

40:54.446 --> 40:58.064
When it became clear
that one side had to go.

40:58.158 --> 41:01.859
One side had to be purged.

41:03.455 --> 41:05.863
I did what I had to do.

41:06.958 --> 41:10.827
I was one of the people that was smart
enough to make sure that I didn't end up

41:10.920 --> 41:12.547
in that ditch.

41:12.630 --> 41:16.551
Which makes me considerably
smarter than you, John.

41:30.315 --> 41:31.858
What did Jacob say to you?

41:31.941 --> 41:33.735
Why did you do this?

41:33.818 --> 41:37.322
Because you heard him.

41:38.531 --> 41:40.857
Now, I need to know what he said.

41:40.950 --> 41:42.410
Help me.

41:42.869 --> 41:47.248
John, I'm not going to ask you again.

41:47.332 --> 41:49.793
What did he say to you?

41:51.628 --> 41:55.924
He said, "Help me."

42:06.810 --> 42:10.814
Well, I certainly hope
he helps you, John.
